{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Python code to Java 8 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following PyPy 3 code to Java 8 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original PyPy 3 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n<your_rewritten_code_1>\ndef solve():\n    n, mod = map(int, input().split())\n    m = n * (n - 1) // 2\n    \n    # Using dictionary-based DP to avoid sparse array allocation\n    dp = [dict() for _ in range(n + 1)]\n    dp1 = [dict() for _ in range(n + 1)]\n    \n    dp[1][m] = 1\n    \n    for i in range(2, n + 1):\n        # Calculate valid range bounds\n        low_bound = m - (i - 1) * (i - 2) // 2\n        high_bound = m + (i - 1) * (i - 2) // 2\n        \n        for x in range(low_bound, high_bound + 1):\n            if x not in dp[i-1]:\n                continue\n            base_val = dp[i-1][x]\n            for d in range(-i + 1, i):\n                new_val = (dp[i].get(x + d, 0) + base_val * (i - abs(d))) % mod\n                dp[i][x + d] = new_val\n    \n    for i in range(2, n + 1):\n        low_bound = m - (i - 1) * (i - 2) // 2\n        high_bound = m + (i - 1) * (i - 2) // 2\n        \n        # First loop: multiply previous dp1 by i\n        for x in range(low_bound, high_bound + 1):\n            if x in dp1[i-1]:\n                dp1[i][x] = (dp1[i-1][x] * i) % mod\n        \n        # Second loop: update with dp values\n        for x in range(low_bound, high_bound + 1):\n            if x not in dp[i-1]:\n                continue\n            base_val = dp[i-1][x]\n            for d in range(1, i):\n                new_x = x - d\n                new_val = (dp1[i].get(new_x, 0) + base_val * (i - d)) % mod\n                dp1[i][new_x] = new_val\n\n    # Sum values beyond m\n    result = 0\n    for x in dp1[-1]:\n        if x > m:\n            result = (result + dp1[-1][x]) % mod\n    return result\n\nimport sys\ninput = lambda: sys.stdin.readline().rstrip()\nprint(solve())\n</your_rewritten_code_1>\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        long n = sc.nextLong();\n        long mod = sc.nextLong();\n        long m = n * (n - 1) / 2;\n        \n        // Using dictionary-based DP to avoid sparse array allocation\n        Map<Long, Long>[] dp = new HashMap[(int)n + 1];\n        Map<Long, Long>[] dp1 = new HashMap[(int)n + 1];\n        \n        for (int i = 0; i <= n; i++) {\n            dp[i] = new HashMap<>();\n            dp1[i] = new HashMap<>();\n        }\n        \n        dp[1].put(m, 1L);\n        \n        for (int i = 2; i <= n; i++) {\n            // Calculate valid range bounds\n            long low_bound = m - (i - 1) * (i - 2) / 2;\n            long high_bound = m + (i - 1) * (i - 2) / 2;\n            \n            for (long x = low_bound; x <= high_bound; x++) {\n                if (!dp[i-1].containsKey(x)) {\n                    continue;\n                }\n                long base_val = dp[i-1].get(x);\n                for (int d = -i + 1; d < i; d++) {\n                    long new_val = (dp[i].getOrDefault(x + d, 0L) + base_val * (i - Math.abs(d))) % mod;\n                    dp[i].put(x + d, new_val);\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        \n        for (int i = 2; i <= n; i++) {\n            long low_bound = m - (i - 1) * (i - 2) / 2;\n            long high_bound = m + (i - 1) * (i - 2) / 2;\n            \n            // First loop: multiply previous dp1 by i\n            for (long x = low_bound; x <= high_bound; x++) {\n                if (dp1[i-1].containsKey(x)) {\n                    dp1[i].put(x, (dp1[i-1].get(x) * i) % mod);\n                }\n            }\n            \n            // Second loop: update with dp values\n            for (long x = low_bound; x <= high_bound; x++) {\n                if (!dp[i-1].containsKey(x)) {\n                    continue;\n                }\n                long base_val = dp[i-1].get(x);\n                for (int d = 1; d < i; d++) {\n                    long new_x = x - d;\n                    long new_val = (dp1[i].getOrDefault(new_x, 0L) + base_val * (i - d)) % mod;\n                    dp1[i].put(new_x, new_val);\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        \n        // Sum values beyond m\n        long result = 0;\n        for (Map.Entry<Long, Long> entry : dp1[(int)n].entrySet()) {\n            if (entry.getKey() > m) {\n                result = (result + entry.getValue()) % mod;\n            }\n        }\n        System.out.println(result);\n    }\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-9.297892393078655e-05, -1.4305104514278355e-06, -1.0728830375228426e-06, -0.0003778220561798662, -2.5748875486897305e-05, -0.25193580985069275, -0.3888787031173706, -7.152531907195225e-06, -5.960462772236497e-07, -4.2437604861333966e-05, -0.04858801141381264, -0.0010336062405258417, -0.013130155391991138, -5.960462772236497e-07, -0.0014887689612805843, -0.011049393564462662, -2.861018856492592e-06, -1.0728830375228426e-06, -7.331102824537084e-05, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -4.017272294731811e-05, -2.0265558760002023e-0